From: NINUX Basilicata
Subject: [PATCH] luci-base: form: ignore denied luci config read on login page

form.js reads the 'luci' config as soon as it is loaded. On the login
page the session is anonymous, rpcd denies uci/get and, since .catch()
without a handler does not catch anything, the rejection ends up in the
browser console as "RPCError: RPC call to uci/get failed with error
-32002: Access denied".

Backport of the form.js hunk of upstream commit a818ac89bb0e
("luci-base: correctness fixes"), not in openwrt-25.12.

diff --git a/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/form.js b/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/form.js
index 3d87b3d7..d2466748 100644
--- a/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/form.js
+++ b/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/form.js
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 
 const scope = this;
 
-uci.loadPackage('luci').catch();
+uci.loadPackage('luci').catch(() => {});
 
 const callSessionAccess = rpc.declare({
 	object: 'session',
